Thank you for reaching out to the Oregon Department of Human Services (ODHS=
) Public Records Unit. We have received your email and appreciate you conta=
cting us.

To request ODHS public records, personal records, or make a media records r=
equest, please complete the ODHS Online Records Request Form<https://www.or=
egon.gov/odhs/pages/records-requests.aspx>.

To request records of major life events for Oregonians such as births, deat=
hs, marriages, divorces, registered domestic partnerships, and more, please=
 contact the Oregon Vital Records Office<https://www.oregon.gov/oha/PH/BIRT=
HDEATHCERTIFICATES/Pages/index.aspx>.

If you are a current or past recipient of ODHS services and need documentat=
ion, please contact your local ODHS office<https://www.oregon.gov/odhs/page=
s/office-finder.aspx?utm_source=3DodHS&utm_medium=3Degov_redirect&utm_campa=
ign=3Dhttps%3A%2F%2Fwww.oregon.gov%2Fdhs%2Foffices%2Fpages%2Findex.aspx%5C&=
serviceid=3D25> for verification requests.

For Out of State Child Welfare Agencies, please email your request on agenc=
y letterhead to recreq.orchildhot@odhs.oregon.gov.<mailto:recreq.orchildhot=
@odhs.oregon.gov>

For all other inquiries, a member of our team will review your message and =
follow up with you. Our current response time is three to four business day=
s.

Thank you,

Public Records Unit
Oregon Department of Human Services
Message Line: 503-945-5617

